Article 6: Where the seller concludes multiple sales contracts for the same ordinary movable property, and all the sales contracts are valid, and all buyers request actual performance of the contract, the matters shall be handled separately according to the following circumstances:
(1) Where the buyer who first took delivery requests confirmation that the ownership has been transferred, the People's Court shall support the claim;
(2) Where none of the buyers has taken delivery, and the buyer who first paid the price requests the seller to perform contractual obligations such as delivery of the subject matter, the People's Court shall support the claim;
(3) Where none of the buyers has taken delivery or paid the price, and the buyer whose contract was legally formed first requests the seller to perform contractual obligations such as delivery of the subject matter, the People's Court shall support the claim.

Article 7: Where the seller concludes multiple sales contracts for the same special movable property such as a ship, aircraft, or motor vehicle, and all the sales contracts are valid, and all buyers request actual performance of the contract, the matters shall be handled separately according to the following circumstances:
(1) Where the buyer who first took delivery requests the seller to perform contractual obligations such as going through the formalities for registration of transfer of ownership, the People's Court shall support the claim;
(2) Where none of the buyers has taken delivery, and the buyer who first went through the formalities for registration of transfer of ownership requests the seller to perform contractual obligations such as delivery of the subject matter, the People's Court shall support the claim;
(3) Where none of the buyers has taken delivery or gone through the formalities for registration of transfer of ownership, and the buyer whose contract was legally formed first requests the seller to perform contractual obligations such as delivery of the subject matter and going through the formalities for registration of transfer of ownership, the People's Court shall support the claim;
(4) Where the seller delivers the subject matter to one of the buyers and also goes through registration of transfer of ownership for another buyer, and the buyer who has taken delivery requests that the ownership of the subject matter be registered in its own name, the People's Court shall support the claim.
III. Risk Bearing of the Subject Matter

Article 30: Where a sales contract contains any of the following agreed contents, it shall not constitute a sale on trial. Where the buyer claims that it is a sale on trial, the People's Court shall not support the claim:
(1) It is agreed that the buyer shall purchase the subject matter when the subject matter meets certain requirements after trial use or inspection;
(2) It is agreed that the buyer shall purchase the subject matter when a third party approves the subject matter after trial;
(3) It is agreed that the buyer may exchange the subject matter within a certain period;
(4) It is agreed that the buyer may return the subject matter within a certain period.
VIII. Other Issues

Article 31: Where the seller, after performing its delivery obligation, files a lawsuit requesting the buyer to pay the price, and the buyer raises an objection on the ground that the seller breached the contract first, the People's Court shall handle the matter separately according to the following circumstances:
(1) Where the buyer refuses to pay liquidated damages, refuses to compensate for losses, or claims that the seller shall take remedial measures such as reducing the price, it constitutes raising a defense;
(2) Where the buyer claims that the seller shall pay liquidated damages, compensate for losses, or requests dissolution of the contract, it shall file a counterclaim.
